# AI UI/UX Generation Rules 

## 1. Core Layout Constraints
* **Screen Fit:** All generated UI components, tables, and dashboards **must fit entirely within standard desktop viewport widths and heights** without requiring vertical or horizontal page scrolling.
* **Shell Consistency:** Always wrap generated content inside the standard layout frame (dark blue vertical sidebar navigation + top status bar).

## 2. Data & Information Hierarchy
* **User Input Priority:** Center the UI strictly around user-inputted fields (e.g., Request Number, Title, Type, Status). 
* **Overflow Handling:** Hide or relocate secondary database metadata (auto-generated IDs, raw timestamps, complex relational foreign keys) into a collapsible **Right-Side Inspector Panel**. Do not crowd the primary data table.

## 3. Visual & Aesthetic Styling
* **Theme Matching:** Use the established Haz360 color palette (dark navy sidebar, clean white/light gray background containers, high-contrast status badge colors like Red for open items, Yellow for WIP, and Blue/Green for completed states).